Z||000000||AL||01-21-2001||10:07 PM||||<BR>well i fixed the fuel pump and the motor works fine on the indy, i let the car idle for a while and then i decided to see if the clutch worked well it worked ok but it seemed(the clutch)kinda hard but i could shift the gear in.well i turned it off and for an hour or so i went back and turned it back on well this time i couldn't get the car in gear at all so my question is how do you know for certain that the clutch is bad or it just needs adjustment,i'm new to the fiero clutch scene,thanks AL.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Bob Englert||01-21-2001||10:20 PM||||I don't know about the clutch internals but the clutch hydralics are a common problem on all Fieros.  Measure the travel of the clutch arm at the rod by the slave cylinder while someone presses the clutch to the floor and back.<P>You should see at least 15/16" of travel.  Ideally you should have about 1.2".  If it is not traveling at least 15/16" you will not be getting complete release of the clutch, causing hard shifting and grinding into 1st and rev.<P>There were several service buletins on the clutch system.  GM replaced the composite clutch arm with a cast arm that is much stiffer.  They repalced the original aluminum clutch pedal which can bend and reduce travel with a steel pedal that is stiffer.  Most owners have had much better luck replacing the master and slave cylinder with original GM parts and not the auto store aftermarket components.  <P>Bleeding the hydralics is and exercise in patience.  Welcome to the fun!<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000002||Motorhead||01-22-2001||05:15 PM||||I gotta' agree with Bob about the master and slave cylinders.  I used to keep a bucket and bleeder hose handy all the time 'till I finally replaced both cylinders with "Genuine GM" parts.  The clutch now works flawlessly, and I don't smell like brake fluid all the time.  Also installed an '84 shifter in the car this weekend.  SWEET!!<BR>Mike<P>------------------<BR>"The one who dies with the most toys wins!"<BR>  bluewater46@hotmail.com<BR>1986 coupe<BR>1984 coupe<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1372350&a=10234998&p=38686771&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||1
